        <headerFormat>TIFF</headerFormat>
        <dataFormat>TIFF</dataFormat>
        <numImagesOrTiltSeries>7943</numImagesOrTiltSeries>
        <framesPerImage>80</framesPerImage>
        <frameRange>
            <frameRangeMin>1</frameRangeMin>
            <frameRangeMax>80</frameRangeMax>
        </frameRange>
        <voxelType>UNSIGNED 16 BIT INTEGER</voxelType>
        <dimensions>
            <imageWidth>3710</imageWidth>
            <pixelWidth>0.667089</pixelWidth>
            <imageHeight>3838</imageHeight>
            <pixelHeight>0.667089</pixelHeight>
        </dimensions>
        <details>Images were recorded in two sessions. This second session was on a Titan Krios electron microscope (FEI) equipped with a K2 summit direct detector operating at 0.667 Å per pixel in counting mode using the Leginon software package. Pixel size was calibrated in-house using a proteasome test sample. Data collection was performed using a dose of ~77.53 e-/Å2 across 80 frames (100 msec per frame) at a dose rate of ~4.3 e–/pix/sec, using a set defocus range of -0.3 μm to -2.9 μm. 100 micron objective aperture was used. The movies were recorded over three days using an image beam shift data collection strategy.

These files have been CTF corrected using the parameters in: data/02_Aligned_Micrographs/micrographs_ctf_19may24c_K2.star</details>
        <segmentationList/>
        <micrographsFilePattern></micrographsFilePattern>
        <pickedParticlesFilePattern></pickedParticlesFilePattern>
        <pickedParticlesDirectory></pickedParticlesDirectory>
    </imageSet>
